From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:18:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the view through strips in DTCM

Writing the view down the columns of the frame misses the data cache
with every pixel, which is slow in DS main RAM. The ray caster only
notes the texture column of each post and ScaleLine queues the sprite
columns over each column of the view instead. Once the weapon is queued
the view is put together in strips of 8 columns in DTCM: the ceiling and
floor filled in words, so the screen isn't cleared first, then the wall
post and the sprite columns over it, and the strip is copied into the
frame in doublewords. The texture steps in 16.16 fixed point through a
copy of its column in DTCM, four pixels per loop, as a branch costs the
ARM9 three cycles. Posts taller than the view are clipped at once.
---
 wl_def.h   |   8 ++++
 wl_draw.c  | 120 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------------
 wl_scale.c |  79 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

